<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Xiaojing of Eastern Wei</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">524–552</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Yuan Shanjian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Xiaojing of Eastern Wei, born Yuan Shanjian, was the only emperor of the Eastern Wei. The general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gao-huan">Gao Huan</a> placed him on the throne as a boy in 534 and moved the court to Ye. Real power lay with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gao">Gao</a> Huan and his sons, and in 550 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wenxuan-of-northern-qi">Gao Yang</a> forced him to abdicate and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-qi">Northern Qi</a>. He was poisoned in 552.</p></div>
